cated XFS filesystem mounted at /srv/data with usrquota, set bsoft=bhard=100m for datauser via xfs_quota, and demonstrated kernel-level enforcement: 60MB write succeeded, 150MB write was hard-blocked by XFS with 'Disk quota exceeded' at exactly 100MB used, then cleaned up leaving quota at 0/100M"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline capture on node1","command_ids":["cmd-e755663cfbd14213"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 1e0cb179-d384-41f8-aa25-9390b31eec45, active /srv/data mount, quota config (datauser 0/100M), fstab entry, and datauser account presence prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement for node1","command_ids":["cmd-7292b4544a6a4557"],"summary":"Issued native 'shutdown -r now'; command acknowledgement returned (stream closed) before the node disconnected, confirming the restart was triggered"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart polling and availability recovery","command_ids":["cmd-aa15f142ddc34f7b","cmd-cead4dab0045431f"],"summary":"First poll timed out (node down/rebooting), second poll succeeded with a fresh uptime, confirming exec access returned after restart"},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery for node1","command_ids":["cmd-b3ad485bcee24ee3"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id 973e294e-ea59-4f62-8a8a-a60c5071b1c2 differs from pre-restart value, proving a genuine reboot occurred. Verified /srv/data fstab mount, datauser account, and XFS quota (Enforcement: ON, 100M soft/hard) all recovered automatically, and re-ran the 150MB write test which was again blocked at exactly 100MB by the filesystem, confirming enforcement survives restart"}]},"ttft_ms":3128,"type":"result","duration_ms":76639,"uuid":"f4e94bf0-26b1-4e08-b97a-2535e2a7b235","ttft_stream_ms":749,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":749,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
